  no key             responses [200, 200, 200]   work done 3 time(s)
  idempotency key    responses [200, 200, 409]   work done 1 time(s)

Three attempts at one request. Without a key the server did the work three times;
with one it did it once, told the overlapping retry to wait, and replayed the stored
result to the late one. The key is chosen by the client, once per logical request,
and reused on every retry of it — which is what makes the retry safe to send.
